449	Exempt payee code.
450	• Generally, individuals (including sole proprietors) are not exempt from
451	backup withholding.
452	• Except as provided below, corporations are exempt from backup
453	withholding for certain payments, including interest and dividends.
454	• Corporations are not exempt from backup withholding for payments
455	made in settlement of payment card or third-party network transactions.
456	• Corporations are not exempt from backup withholding with respect to
457	attorneys’ fees or gross proceeds paid to attorneys, and corporations
458	that provide medical or health care services are not exempt with respect
459	to payments reportable on Form 1099-MISC.
460	The following codes identify payees that are exempt from backup
461	withholding. Enter the appropriate code in the space on line 4.
462	1—An organization exempt from tax under section 501(a), any IRA, or
463	a custodial account under section 403(b)(7) if the account satisfies the
464	requirements of section 401(f)(2).
