533	Exemption from FATCA reporting code. The following codes identify
534	payees that are exempt from reporting under FATCA. These codes
535	apply to persons submitting this form for accounts maintained outside
536	of the United States by certain foreign financial institutions. Therefore, if
537	you are only submitting this form for an account you hold in the United
538	States, you may leave this field blank. Consult with the person
539	requesting this form if you are uncertain if the financial institution is
540	subject to these requirements. A requester may indicate that a code is
541	not required by providing you with a Form W-9 with “Not Applicable” (or
542	any similar indication) entered on the line for a FATCA exemption code.
543	A—An organization exempt from tax under section 501(a) or any
544	individual retirement plan as defined in section 7701(a)(37).
545	B—The United States or any of its agencies or instrumentalities.
546	C—A state, the District of Columbia, a U.S. commonwealth or
547	territory, or any of their political subdivisions or instrumentalities.
548	D—A corporation the stock of which is regularly traded on one or
549	more established securities markets, as described in Regulations
550	section 1.1472-1(c)(1)(i).
551	E—A corporation that is a member of the same expanded affiliated
552	group as a corporation described in Regulations section 1.1472-1(c)(1)(i).
553	
554	F—A dealer in securities, commodities, or derivative financial
555	instruments (including notional principal contracts, futures, forwards,
556	and options) that is registered as such under the laws of the United
557	States or any state.
558	G—A real estate investment trust.
559	H—A regulated investment company as defined in section 851 or an
