631	Part II. Certification
632	
633	For this type of account:
634	
635	To establish to the withholding agent that you are a U.S. person, or
636	resident alien, sign Form W-9. You may be requested to sign by the
637	withholding agent even if item 1, 4, or 5 below indicates otherwise.
638	For a joint account, only the person whose TIN is shown in Part I
639	should sign (when required). In the case of a disregarded entity, the
640	person identified on line 1 must sign. Exempt payees, see Exempt payee
641	code, earlier.
642	Signature requirements. Complete the certification as indicated in
643	items 1 through 5 below.
644	1. Interest, dividend, and barter exchange accounts opened
645	before 1984 and broker accounts considered active during 1983.
646	You must give your correct TIN, but you do not have to sign the
647	certification.
648	2. Interest, dividend, broker, and barter exchange accounts
649	opened after 1983 and broker accounts considered inactive during
650	1983. You must sign the certification or backup withholding will apply. If
651	you are subject to backup withholding and you are merely providing
652	your correct TIN to the requester, you must cross out item 2 in the
653	certification before signing the form.
654	3. Real estate transactions. You must sign the certification. You may
655	cross out item 2 of the certification.
656	4. Other payments. You must give your correct TIN, but you do not
657	have to sign the certification unless you have been notified that you
658	have previously given an incorrect TIN. “Other payments” include
659	payments made in the course of the requester’s trade or business for
660	rents, royalties, goods (other than bills for merchandise), medical and
661	health care services (including payments to corporations), payments to
662	a nonemployee for services, payments made in settlement of payment
663	card and third-party network transactions, payments to certain fishing
664	boat crew members and fishermen, and gross proceeds paid to
665	attorneys (including payments to corporations).
666	5. Mortgage interest paid by you, acquisition or abandonment of
667	secured property, cancellation of debt, qualified tuition program
668	payments (under section 529), ABLE accounts (under section 529A),
669	IRA, Coverdell ESA, Archer MSA or HSA contributions or
670	distributions, and pension distributions. You must give your correct
671	TIN, but you do not have to sign the certification.
