845	Privacy Act Notice
846	Section 6109 of the Internal Revenue Code requires you to provide your
847	correct TIN to persons (including federal agencies) who are required to
848	file information returns with the IRS to report interest, dividends, or
849	certain other income paid to you; mortgage interest you paid; the
850	acquisition or abandonment of secured property; the cancellation of
851	debt; or contributions you made to an IRA, Archer MSA, or HSA. The
852	person collecting this form uses the information on the form to file
853	information returns with the IRS, reporting the above information.
854	Routine uses of this information include giving it to the Department of
855	Justice for civil and criminal litigation and to cities, states, the District of
856	Columbia, and U.S. commonwealths and territories for use in
857	administering their laws. The information may also be disclosed to other
858	countries under a treaty, to federal and state agencies to enforce civil
859	and criminal laws, or to federal law enforcement and intelligence
860	agencies to combat terrorism. You must provide your TIN whether or not
861	you are required to file a tax return. Under section 3406, payors must
862	generally withhold a percentage of taxable interest, dividends, and
863	certain other payments to a payee who does not give a TIN to the payor.
864	Certain penalties may also apply for providing false or fraudulent
865	information.
